<!-- Thinlet (modernized) — the GUI-mode XML dialect, as a DTD. TEST RESOURCE.

     Generated from DescriptorTable.WIDGETS and Thinlet.addImpl and regenerated
     on every run by XmlDialectGrammarTest, which fails when this file and the
     code disagree. Never shipped: the published artifact is the byte-identical
     2005 src/main/resources/thinlet.dtd (DECISIONS.md D8), which this file
     deliberately does not match. The divergences are catalogued in
     project-docs/backend-portability/XML-DIALECT.md (DECISIONS.md D96).

     Content models are mixed and unordered because the parser is: it checks
     each parent/child pair on its own (Thinlet.addImpl) and enforces neither
     order nor cardinality, and it tolerates text anywhere (discarding it in
     GUI mode — KNOWN-QUIRKS Q16).

     Attributes are CDATA #IMPLIED throughout: this grammar pins element
     structure and attribute NAMES only. The value layer — types, enumerated
     tokens, defaults — is single-homed in DescriptorTable and pinned by
     DescriptorContractTest and PublicVocabularyContractTest (D57).
     Attribute order is the resolution order of Thinlet.getDefinition: an
     element's own rows first, then each ancestor's, deduplicated so that a
     shadowing row (button's own `alignment`) appears once, where it wins.

     The five predefined XML entities are deliberately NOT declared here.
     -->

